+## Changed
+
+- `src/core/lifecycle/retry.ts`: added `refuseRunningTask`, which reads
+  `.run/running/<n>.pid`, parses a numeric `pid`, and asks `isPidRunning` from
+  `src/core/run/lock.ts`. A lock whose pid no longer runs now refuses with
+  `Task <n> was left running by a stopped watcher (pid <pid>); run osq watch to
+  reap it, then osq retry <id> <n> if it stays dead.`; a lock whose pid runs or
+  whose bytes are not JSON with a numeric `pid` still refuses with `Task <n> is
+  running; retry is refused.` The numeric branch of the existing running-state
+  check calls it; the change target's refusal is untouched. Tagged `retrySpec`
+  with `@scenario watcher-and-harness: Lock of a stopped watcher`,
+  `@scenario watcher-and-harness: Killed watcher's task resumed`, and `@adr 003`.
+- `tests/recovery-killed-watcher-child.ts`: a script, not a test. Given the
+  repo, worktree root, and ready-file path it calls `runWatcherOnce` with
+  `recoveryConfig(worktreeRoot, 1)` and an adapter whose spawn writes `half\n`
+  to the task's first scope file, writes the ready file, then returns a promise
+  that never resolves.
+- `tests/recovery-killed-watcher.test.ts`: proves watcher-and-harness "Killed
+  watcher's task resumed". It approves the shared one-task project, spawns the
+  child with `process.execPath`, `--import tsx` (via `createRequire`) and
+  `--import tests/git-test-env.ts`, polls for the ready file, SIGKILLs the child
+  and awaits its exit, asserts `.run/running/1.pid` remains, `osq retry 1` exits
+  1 with `Task 1 was left running by a stopped watcher (pid <pid>)` and leaves
+  the lock and `.run/dead/` byte-identical, then a `ScriptedAdapter` writing
+  `good\n` spawns once during `watchOnce`, the archived folder holds
+  `.run/dead/1.1.md` with `reason: crashed` and `.run/done/1`, and `osq land`
+  exits 0 with `good\n` in the checkout and a clean status.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- The task set the scope on `retry.ts` while requiring it to stay under the
+  250-line budget. My first pass reached 256 (split-count 257), so I trimmed the
+  doc comment above `retrySpec` to the three tag lines only and kept the
+  `refuseRunningTask` body compact, removing the blank line between
+  `listDir` and it. The file ends at 249 newlines / 250 split lines, exactly the
+  budget, and biome accepts the formatting.
+- `recovery-killed-watcher.test.ts` derives the child's worktree root from
+  `project.config.vcs?.worktreeRoot` with a `path.dirname(repo)/worktrees`
+  fallback, because `createRecoveryProject` does not return the temp worktree
+  root directly.
+
+## Missing context
+
+None — task 1's `tests/recovery-support.ts` provided everything needed.
+
+## Next
+
+None — every acceptance line is met, the task verify passes, and `pnpm verify`
+exits 0.
+
+Touched: src/core/lifecycle/retry.ts, tests/recovery-killed-watcher-child.ts, tests/recovery-killed-watcher.test.ts
